[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:The End of a Dream]
[00:01.52]How did the dream end? | 这个梦是怎样结束的呢？
[00:14.18]Tired of sleeping on the floor, | 德黑兰有个年轻人，他睡在地板上，感到厌倦，
[00:17.82]a young man in Teheran saved up for years to buy a real bed. | 于是积蓄了好几年，买了一张真正的床。
[00:24.38]For the first time in his life, | 他生平第一次
[00:27.86]he became the proud owner of a bed which had springs and a mattress. | 拥有了一张带弹簧和床垫的床，他为此感到十分自豪。
[00:34.60]Because the weather was very hot, | 因为天气很热，
[00:38.38]he carried the bed on to the roof of his house. | 他便把床搬到了屋顶上。
[00:42.85]He slept very well for the first two nights, | 头两晚他睡得很好，
[00:47.62]but on the third night, a storm blew up. | 但第三天晚上，暴风雨突然降临。
[00:52.38]A gust of wind swept the bed off the roof and sent it crashing into the courtyard below. | 一阵狂风把床从屋顶上刮了下来，摔到了下面的院子里。
[01:01.48]The young man did not wake up | 那个年轻人直到
[01:04.34]until the bed had struck the ground. | 床撞到地上才醒过来。
[01:07.74]Although the bed was smashed to pieces, | 尽管床摔成了碎片，
[01:11.74]the man was miraculously unhurt. | 但那个人却奇迹般地没有受伤。
[01:15.68]When he woke up, he was still on the mattress. | 他醒来时，仍然躺在床垫上。
[01:20.44]Glancing at the bits of wood and metal that lay around him, | 他看了一眼周围的木头和金属碎片，
[01:25.37]the man sadly picked up the mattress and carried it into his house. | 伤心地抱起床垫，把它搬进了屋里。
[01:31.33]After he had put it on the floor, | 他把床垫放到地板上，
[01:34.40]he promptly went to sleep again. | 便很快又睡着了。